# The graphics drivers Nix apps use: Mesa from NixOS's stable release, as a
# store path from cache.nixos.org (kosher-nix-opengl.service fetches it and
# /run/opengl-driver points at it).
#
# A Nix build brings its own OpenGL loader, and that loader looks for the
# drivers in /run/opengl-driver, as on NixOS. Fedora has nothing there, so
# kitty, Alacritty, Ghostty and Cool Retro Term from nixpkgs could not open
# a window even with the machine's own drivers working (#157).
#
# Stable, not unstable, on purpose. A driver is loaded into the app's own
# process, so it must not need a newer C library than the app was built
# with. Apps from the Store come from nixpkgs-unstable, which is always
# newer than the stable release, so they can all load this driver.
#
# Bump with scripts/nix-opengl-pin.sh after a NixOS release.
# nixos-26.05 26f4107e47e3ad0ffd0db220469ba83b6f6d96e8
KOSHER_OPENGL_DRIVER=/nix/store/ij4mv4rzvd60yql6jafpmh95x3l63937-mesa-26.1.8
